I wanna see myself forever.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.256
- Alright, Tim clearly establishing

00:06:55.256 --> 00:06:56.714
on the show it's all about Tim.

00:06:56.714 --> 00:06:57.778
Britt?

00:06:57.778 --> 00:06:59.985
- Instagram, hands down.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:02.054
- Instagram, I like Instagram.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:05.062
- Yeah, so for me, I would
probably buy Snapchat.

00:07:05.062 --> 00:07:07.559
And here's why, because of those answers.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:10.632
I truly believe that Instagram
is the social network

00:07:10.632 --> 00:07:11.862
of the moment.

00:07:11.862 --> 00:07:14.732
When I buy things, I
like to buy for 24, 36,

00:07:14.732 --> 00:07:16.990
48 months out, when I invest.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.707
The way I built Vayner
Media, we were selling

00:07:18.707 --> 00:07:21.113
social media in 2009 and
10, you remember this,

00:07:21.113 --> 00:07:22.466
like, people didn't want to buy this

00:07:22.466 --> 00:07:24.090
as much as they want to buy it now.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.284
I like projecting.

00:07:25.284 --> 00:07:26.967
Plus there's one other
thing about Snapchat

00:07:26.967 --> 00:07:28.790
that makes me give this answer.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:32.775
Snapchat is a, I think that Instagram

00:07:32.775 --> 00:07:35.408
was a moving the ball forward

00:07:35.408 --> 00:07:37.580
in a Facebook, Twitter world.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.202
I think Snapchat is a complete
different paradigm shift.

00:07:40.202 --> 00:07:42.311
If it's a completely
different way to communicate.

00:07:42.311 --> 00:07:43.969
It's got different functionality.

00:07:43.969 --> 00:07:45.966
30 to 40 year olds that have never used it

00:07:45.966 --> 00:07:48.385
are completely confused by it.

00:07:48.385 --> 00:07:49.595
I'm fascinated by that,

00:07:49.595 --> 00:07:52.073
that also feels to me like
there's a lot of upside.

00:07:52.073 --> 00:07:53.730
I think a lot of 30, 40, 50 year olds

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.691
understand how to use Instagram.

00:07:55.691 --> 00:07:57.613
It's very native, it's
basically like Facebook,

00:07:57.613 --> 00:07:58.825
boom, they're there, that's good.

00:07:58.825 --> 00:08:00.429
That's the vulnerability of Snapchat,

00:08:00.429 --> 00:08:01.407
but I also think that's the upside.

00:08:01.407 --> 00:08:03.503
If explained properly,

00:08:03.503 --> 00:08:05.882
which I think Twitter never
really fully accomplished,

00:08:05.882 --> 00:08:08.214
I think Snapchat becomes a beast.

00:08:08.214 --> 00:08:09.788
For me, watching the behavior,

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:11.787
Snapchat is chipping
away on a daily basis.

00:08:11.787 --> 00:08:14.078
And only because of the way
I like to buy businesses,

00:08:14.078 --> 00:08:16.468
which is, what do I think
is the number one play,

00:08:16.468 --> 00:08:18.402
24, 36 months from now?

00:08:18.402 --> 00:08:19.212
It's Snapchat.

00:08:19.212 --> 00:08:20.845
That being said, I'm hedging against that,

00:08:20.845 --> 00:08:23.465
I'm not sold that Snapchat
is the biggest social network

00:08:23.465 --> 00:08:25.672
24, 36 months from now,
because I do believe

00:08:25.672 --> 00:08:28.802
the Facebook, Instagram,
you know, WhatsApp,

00:08:28.802 --> 00:08:31.124
you know, Facebook Messenger monster

00:08:31.124 --> 00:08:33.952
is in its early stages.

00:08:33.952 --> 00:08:36.024
I am as bullish on
Facebook as I've ever been.

00:08:36.024 --> 00:08:39.458
And so that's my answer,
that's my rationale.

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:43.203
- [Voiceover] Amanda asks, 
"Do you use a meal prep service?

00:08:43.203 --> 00:08:46.774
"What do you think the future
of services like that is?"

