Like I really think that
infrastructure's gonna be here.

00:09:27.985 --> 00:09:30.599
I don't think people really
project technology well.

00:09:30.599 --> 00:09:32.509
Meaning, in 20 years from today,

00:09:32.509 --> 00:09:34.844
so many of your jobs will be obsolete.

00:09:34.844 --> 00:09:36.706
So much technology will eat up

00:09:36.706 --> 00:09:38.244
the jobs that so many people do,

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:40.180
at a minimum wage, or lower income,

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.913
that a lot of those same jobs,

00:09:41.913 --> 00:09:45.155
in the same way that a
lot of Uber drivers today

00:09:45.155 --> 00:09:46.889
used to do something else

00:09:46.889 --> 00:09:48.554
that's been replaced by technology,

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.268
when they were making 48,000 a year,

00:09:50.268 --> 00:09:51.478
but now as an Uber driver they're making

00:09:51.478 --> 00:09:53.163
92,000 a year.

00:09:53.163 --> 00:09:54.506
So everyone's like, oh, this is so bad,

00:09:54.506 --> 00:09:57.199
we're gonna put, you
know, these developers

00:09:57.199 --> 00:09:59.921
out of business, or film
developers out of business,

00:09:59.921 --> 00:10:01.183
or whatever it may be.

00:10:01.183 --> 00:10:05.378
Yes, but then all sorts of
things get created that are new.

00:10:05.378 --> 00:10:08.246
Too many people are
just so half glass full.

00:10:08.246 --> 00:10:10.340
Too many people are so doomsday, like,

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:13.246
when India wants her
goddamn radishes right now,

